{"sections":{"oniguruma-parser 🌿":"oniguruma-parser is a TypeScript library for parsing, validating, traversing, transforming, and optimizing Oniguruma regular expressions. It has been tested extensively through Oniguruma-To-ES and tm-grammars, which Shiki uses to process tens of thousands of real-world patterns.","📜 Contents":"The contents list links to installation, AST parsing, traversal and transformation, pattern generation, and regex optimization. It also links to known differences and the supported Oniguruma version.","Additional modules":"Beyond its root export, the library provides parser, traverser, generator, and optimizer modules. These expose AST construction and parsing utilities, AST traversal and transformation, pattern and flag generation, and regex optimization.","🌲 Convert a pattern to an AST":"The toOnigurumaAst function parses a pattern into an OnigurumaAst, accepting optional flags and captureGroup or singleline rules and throwing errors for invalid patterns or flags. It wraps the parser module's parse function and automatically supplies Unicode property validation data.","🌀 Traverse and transform an AST":"The traverser module supports traversing and transforming an OnigurumaAst. Its linked README provides details and examples.","↩️ Convert an AST to a pattern":"The generator module converts an OnigurumaAst into pattern and flags strings. Its linked README provides details and examples.","🪄 Optimize regexes":"The optimizer can minify regexes and improve their performance and readability while preserving exactly which strings they match. The section demonstrates a substantial simplification and links to the optimizer documentation and an interactive demo.","🆚 Known differences":"The library has documented unsupported features and behavioral differences from Oniguruma. The README states that these differences will be resolved in future versions.","Unsupported features":"Unsupported features include rare character escapes, code point sequences, certain absence expressions, conditionals, non-built-in callouts, some backreferences, and certain flag placements, though a sample of roughly 55,000 TextMate regexes showed more than 99.99% support. The section also documents missing validation errors, explains restrictions on numbered forward backreferences, and identifies planned CharacterSequence, Conditional, and Callout AST node types.","Behavior differences":"Behavioral differences concern the digit limit for unenclosed backreferences and stricter handling of several Oniguruma edge cases. The library rejects certain constructs associated with engine bugs or undefined behavior rather than reproducing those outcomes.","Unenclosed four-digit backreferences":"Unenclosed backreferences support at most three digits, so \\1000 is parsed as \\100 followed by a literal 0 even when enough preceding capture groups exist. Enclosed backreferences have no such digit limit, while the README notes that tested vscode-oniguruma versions fail to match patterns containing more than 999 captures.","Erroring on patterns that trigger Oniguruma bugs":"The library throws errors for nested absence functions, bare \\x, incomplete \\u, and invalid standalone encoded bytes rather than reproducing Oniguruma bugs or undefined behavior. Future versions are intended to accept nested absence functions and follow legitimate Oniguruma rules for \\x while continuing to exclude buggy behavior.","🔢 Oniguruma version":"All library versions to date follow Oniguruma 6.9.10, released January 1, 2025, with Unicode 16.0.0. Syntax changes have generally been backward compatible since at least version 6.0.0, and differences from the widely used vscode-oniguruma baseline of 6.9.8 are described as negligible.","🧩 Contributing":"Contributions to the project are welcome. A linked contribution guide explains how to get started.","🏷️ About":"The project was created by Steven Levithan and contributors and is distributed under the MIT License with a 2025–present copyright notice. Readers are encouraged to support it through improvements, sharing, or sponsorship.","Sponsors and backers":"The section recognizes Roboflow as a sponsor or backer. Its linked avatar points to Roboflow's GitHub profile.","Past sponsors":"The section recognizes antfu and brc-dd as past sponsors. The closing text invites contributions, sharing, and sponsorship of ongoing development."},"concerns":[],"rationale":"Read README.md and provided exactly two sentences for every Markdown heading except Install and use; Additional modules is included as its own titled subsection, while expandable details are summarized within their parent sections."}

