{"sections":{"magic-string":"magic-string is a small, fast utility for modifying source strings and generating source maps. It is intended for lightweight edits where parsing and rewriting an abstract syntax tree would be unnecessary or unsuitable.","Usage":"Create a MagicString instance, edit it using original-string character indices, and serialize the result with toString(). The examples also demonstrate generating a version 3 source map and supplying constructor options for filenames, indentation exclusions, debugger ignore-listing, and position offsets.","Properties":"The Properties section documents the offset property. This property adjusts incoming positions for several editing and slicing APIs.","s.offset":"The offset property shifts incoming positions for slice, update, overwrite, insertion, move, reset, and remove operations. The example sets an offset of six so that slicing 'hello world' returns 'world'.","Methods":"The Methods section describes string editing, inspection, cloning, trimming, and source-map generation APIs. Individual entries explain original-position indexing, chaining, options, restrictions, and deprecated alternatives.","s.addSourcemapLocation( index )":"Adds a character index from the original string to the source-map mappings. This applies when high-resolution mapping is disabled.","s.append( content )":"Appends the supplied content to the end of the string. It returns the instance for chaining.","s.appendLeft( index, content )":"Appends content at an original-string index and associates it with a range ending at that index if the range is later moved. It returns the instance and differs from prependLeft in insertion ordering.","s.appendRight( index, content )":"Appends content at an original-string index and associates it with a range starting at that index if the range is later moved. It returns the instance and differs from prependRight in insertion ordering.","s.clone()":"Creates a clone of the MagicString instance. The README describes this method briefly without additional options or examples.","s.generateDecodedMap( options )":"Generates a source-map object whose mappings are raw arrays rather than an encoded string. It accepts the same options as generateMap and is useful for further map manipulation.","s.generateMap( options )":"Generates a version 3 source map with optional file, source, original-content inclusion, and mapping-resolution settings, including character-level or word-boundary mappings. The returned map provides toString() for JSON serialization and toUrl() for a data URI.","s.hasChanged()":"Reports whether the string has been changed. This provides a direct check for modifications.","s.indent( prefix[, options] )":"Prefixes each line with a supplied indentation string, or guesses indentation from the original content and falls back to a tab. It returns the instance and supports excluding specified character ranges from indentation.","s.insertLeft( index, content )":"This method has been deprecated since version 0.17. Use s.appendLeft(...) instead.","s.insertRight( index, content )":"This method has been deprecated since version 0.17. Use s.prependRight(...) instead.","s.isEmpty()":"Reports whether the resulting source is empty. Whitespace is disregarded when determining emptiness.","s.locate( index )":"This method has been deprecated since version 0.10. The README links to pull request #30 for context.","s.locateOrigin( index )":"This method has been deprecated since version 0.10. The README links to pull request #30 for context.","s.move( start, end, index )":"Moves the specified character range to the given index. It returns the instance for chaining.","s.overwrite( start, end, content[, options] )":"Replaces a range and its appended or prepended content, subject to the same restrictions as remove, and returns the instance. Optional storeName and contentOnly settings control source-map name storage and preservation of inserted content, with update suggested when such content should be retained.","s.prepend( content )":"Prepends the supplied content to the string. It returns the instance for chaining.","s.prependLeft ( index, content )":"Behaves like appendLeft at the specified original-string index. Its inserted content precedes any previous appends or prepends at that index.","s.prependRight ( index, content )":"Behaves like appendRight at the specified original-string index. Its inserted content precedes any previous appends or prepends at that index.","s.replace( regexpOrString, substitution )":"Replaces matches of a string or regular expression using a string or function substitution and returns the instance. Unlike native String.replace, it always matches the original string and mutates the MagicString state, so clone first if an independent result is needed.","s.replaceAll( regexpOrString, substitution )":"Behaves like replace but replaces all matching strings and returns the instance. Regular expressions must have the global flag or the method throws a TypeError, matching native replaceAll behavior.","s.remove( start, end )":"Removes a range identified by indices in the original string and returns the instance. Removing the same content twice or making partially overlapping removals causes an error.","s.reset( start, end )":"Resets a range identified by indices in the original string. It can restore removed characters and discard unwanted edits.","s.slice( start, end )":"Returns generated content corresponding to a range in the original string. It throws an error if the supplied indices refer to characters that have already been removed.","s.snip( start, end )":"Returns a clone restricted to the selected original-string range. Content outside that range is removed from the clone.","s.toString()":"Returns the generated string. This serializes the current edited content.","s.trim([ charType ])":"Trims matching content from both the start and end of the string. The pattern defaults to whitespace, and the method returns the instance.","s.trimStart([ charType ])":"Trims matching content from the start of the string. The pattern defaults to whitespace, and the method returns the instance.","s.trimEnd([ charType ])":"Trims matching content from the end of the string. The pattern defaults to whitespace, and the method returns the instance.","s.trimLines()":"Removes empty lines from the beginning and end of the string. It returns the instance for chaining.","s.update( start, end, content[, options] )":"Replaces a range subject to remove's restrictions and returns the instance, preserving appended or prepended content by default. Optional storeName and overwrite settings control source-map name storage and replacement of inserted content, and the default operation is equivalent to overwrite with contentOnly enabled.","Bundling":"MagicString.Bundle concatenates multiple sources, supporting filenames, indentation exclusions, debugger ignore-list metadata, wrapping, and combined source-map generation. Sources can be added as descriptor objects or directly as MagicString instances when relevant metadata is unnecessary or already supplied to the constructor.","License":"The project is licensed under the MIT license. This section contains no additional licensing details."},"concerns":[],"rationale":"Read README.md and provided two-sentence summaries keyed by every section and subsection title, excluding Installation as assigned."}

