{"sections":{"mdast-util-gfm-table":"This package provides mdast extensions for parsing and serializing GitHub Flavored Markdown tables. The introduction also links to project status, package statistics, sponsorship, and community resources.","What is this?":"The package adds GFM table syntax support to mdast through two extensions. They integrate with mdast-util-from-markdown for parsing and mdast-util-to-markdown for serialization.","When to use this":"Use these extensions with the mdast parsing and serialization utilities, combining parsing with micromark-extension-gfm-table. Alternatives include micromark for processing without a syntax tree, mdast-util-gfm for complete GFM support, remark-gfm for higher-level transformations, and mdast-util-to-hast for HTML conversion.","Install":"The package is ESM-only and can be installed with npm on Node.js 16 or newer. Deno and browser examples import version 2 through esm.sh, with the browser example using a bundled module.","Use":"The example parses a Markdown table using the micromark and mdast extensions, then serializes the resulting tree back to Markdown. It demonstrates column alignment and uneven row lengths, with serialization padding missing cells and accommodating an extra column.","API":"The package exports gfmTableFromMarkdown and gfmTableToMarkdown as named exports. It has no default export.","`gfmTableFromMarkdown`":"This function creates an extension that enables GFM table parsing in mdast-util-from-markdown. Its return value is a FromMarkdownExtension.","`gfmTableFromMarkdown` / Returns":"The function returns an extension for mdast-util-from-markdown. The extension enables GFM tables and has the FromMarkdownExtension type.","`gfmTableToMarkdown(options?)`":"This function creates an extension that enables GFM table serialization in mdast-util-to-markdown. It accepts optional configuration and returns a ToMarkdownExtension.","Parameters":"The optional options argument configures the table serialization extension. Its type is Options.","`gfmTableToMarkdown(options?)` / Returns":"The function returns an extension for mdast-util-to-markdown. The extension enables GFM tables and has the ToMarkdownExtension type.","`Options`":"Options is the TypeScript configuration type for table serialization. It controls cell padding, delimiter alignment, and the function used to measure cell content length.","Fields":"tableCellPadding and tablePipeAlign are booleans that both default to true and control padding and delimiter alignment. stringLength measures cell content for alignment and defaults to JavaScript string length.","Examples":"This section presents an example of customizing table alignment through stringLength. It contrasts default string-length measurement with visual-width measurement for full-width characters and emoji.","Example: `stringLength`":"Default string-length measurement can produce visually misaligned tables containing Chinese characters or emoji. Passing string-width as the stringLength option improves alignment by measuring the visual width of cell content.","HTML":"This utility does not convert Markdown to HTML. The README directs users to mdast-util-to-hast for that conversion.","Syntax":"The README delegates table syntax documentation to micromark-extension-gfm-table. It links directly to that package's Syntax section.","Syntax tree":"The utility adds table-related interfaces to mdast. This section documents nodes, alignment values, and content models.","Nodes":"The table node hierarchy consists of Table, TableRow, and TableCell. These represent a table, its rows, and the header or data cells within each row.","`Table`":"Table is a Parent node representing two-dimensional data, with tableRow children and an optional list of column alignments. It belongs to flow content, and its first child represents the column labels.","`TableRow`":"TableRow is a Parent node representing a row of tableCell children. When it is the first child of a Table, it represents the table's column labels.","`TableCell`":"TableCell is a Parent node representing a header cell when its parent is the table's first row, or a data cell otherwise. Its children are phrasing content excluding Break nodes.","Enumeration":"This section defines the alignType enumeration used for table column alignment. Its values are center, left, right, and null.","`alignType`":"alignType specifies how phrasing content is aligned using left, right, or center values corresponding to CSS text-align. A null value leaves alignment to the host environment.","Content model":"The content models add Table to flow content and define which nodes may appear inside tables and rows. TableContent consists of TableRow, while RowContent consists of TableCell.","`FlowContent` (GFM table)":"FlowContentGfm extends the existing flow content model with Table. Its definition is the union of Table and FlowContent.","`TableContent`":"TableContent is defined as TableRow. It represents the rows contained in a table.","`RowContent`":"RowContent is defined as TableCell. It represents the cells contained in a row.","Types":"The package is fully typed with TypeScript and exports the Options type. The Table, TableRow, and TableCell node types are provided by @types/mdast.","Compatibility":"The unified collective targets maintained Node.js versions and drops unmaintained versions in new major releases, with this package's version 2 line targeting Node.js 16 compatibility. The utility works with version 2 or newer of both mdast-util-from-markdown and mdast-util-to-markdown.","Related":"Related packages include remark-gfm for remark-based GFM support and mdast-util-gfm for all GFM syntax-tree extensions. micromark-extension-gfm-table supplies the corresponding table parsing extension for micromark.","Contribute":"Contribution and support guidance are linked from the syntax-tree organization's shared community files. Participation in the repository, organization, or community requires adherence to its code of conduct.","License":"The package is licensed under MIT. The copyright attribution names Titus Wormer."},"concerns":["Two subsections share the title Returns, so their keys are qualified by their parent API heading to avoid duplicate JSON keys."],"rationale":"Read README.md and summarized every heading-defined section except Contents in two sentences, including nested sections and the introductory project section."}

